# Alembic Migrations

This directory contains the Alembic migration environment for the
CloudScale AI backend.

## How to use

All commands must be run from the `backend/` directory with the virtual
environment activated.

### Generate a migration (autogenerate from models)

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Initial migration"

### Apply all pending migrations

    alembic upgrade head

### Other useful commands

    alembic downgrade -1                  # Revert the last migration
    alembic history                       # Show migration history
    alembic current                       # Show current revision
    alembic check                         # Check for pending model changes

## Configuration notes

- The database URL is loaded automatically from `app.core.config.settings`
  (sourced from `backend/.env`) — it is **not** stored in `alembic.ini`.
- `target_metadata = Base.metadata` is wired to `app.db.base.Base`, so
  `--autogenerate` will reflect any ORM models imported by the app.

